# The list follows from the program alone. Whether a match is entered at all hangs on the most that it could cost, and that counts the ways through the choices of the pattern:
# the alternatives of a group once where it stands once, once for each character where it is repeated.
# new RegExp("a" + /^(?:a|aa)+b/.test("a".repeat(30))): two to the power of thirty ways: not entered . ("b" + /^(?:a|aa)+b/.test("aaaab")): entered
# ("c" + /^(?:a|aa)(?:a|aa) .. 34 in a row .. b/.test("a".repeat(50))): not entered . ("d" + /^(?:get|put)-(?:one|all)$/.test("put-all")): entered
# ("e" + /^(?:a|a) .. 32 in a row .. (?:(?:a|a) .. 32 more ..)b/.test("b")): two to the power of 64 ways, which is more than a word holds: not entered
# DIAGNOSTIC: RegExpPatternNotConstant
# RUN: regexp-texts mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: text /afalse/
# CHECK: text /btrue/
# CHECK-NOT: text /cfalse/
# CHECK: text /dtrue/
# CHECK-NOT: text /efalse/

